f New Music","episode":"Spectacular Acts of Self Sabotage","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UH3n1oQSOc0"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"The Smashing Pumpkins' second album, *Siamese Dream*, was released on July 19, 1993, in the UK and a week later in North America. Billy Corgan initially envisioned an \"outsider artist\" creating an avant-garde, untrained, but passionate cover that might not be widely understood or liked, but this idea was rejected by the label. Instead, a photograph by Melody McDaniel featuring two seven-year-old child models, Ali Langer and Los Angeles Roberts, was chosen. The girls, who had never met before but displayed instant chemistry, were photographed in Los Angeles. They were kept smiling with popsicles from a passing ice cream truck and only settled down when promised they could keep the shoes they were trying on. \"The label rejected the idea and a photo of two little girls was selected.\"","year":1993,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Stories Behind Iconic Album Covers Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sn5TWBFd0XM"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"The album from which the song \"Rockets\" features Billy Corgan playing one of his favorite Fender Stratocasters. \"The smashing pumpkins with rockets from the Simeez Dream album featuring Billy Corgan playing one of his favorite Fender Stratocasters.\"","year":1993,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Story of the Electric Guitar - Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E6cXyaHALBQ"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album debuted at number 10 on the album chart and achieved multi-platinum status. It generated a string of top 10 modern rock singles, including \"Cherub Rock,\" \"Disarm,\" and \"Today,\" following the band's ascent to platinum status after the Seattle bands' breakthrough. \"Their 1993 album, Siamese Dream, debuted at number 10 on the album chart, went multi-platinum.\"","year":1993,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"All Apologies Edition Part 1","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4ef5154465cd600c4fb2"},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"All Apologies Edition Part 1","url":null}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album represents the \"glory days\" of The Smashing Pumpkins. It was released after D'Arcy Wretzky and James Iha had broken up their romantic relationship but continued to work together in the band. \"Here are the pumpkins from the glory days of the Siamese Dream album after Darcy and James broke up, but before the horse farm, the massage is on the crack.\"","year":1993,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Your questions answered","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zUQ2vZzmRiI"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":139962594214217,"artist":"Smashing Pumpkins","artist_id":42147382330261,"title":"Siamese Dream","year":1993,"ess":0,"yt":"3bpRx22whPc","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Grunge","scene_id":32992220995517,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#grunge","chapters":["Sección 6.12"],"pages":[[1,276,null]]}],"others":[{"id":164151696015749,"type":"album","name":"Mellon Collie and the Infinite Sadness","year":1995,"weight":117},{"id":248744582297546,"type":"album","name":"Gish","year":1991,"weight":60},{"id":153700287596985,"type":"album","name":"Machina, The Machines of God","year":2000,"weight":34},{"id":145519503998192,"type":"album","name":"Adore","year":1998,"weight":32},{"id":231096191157557,"type":"song","name":"Bullet with Butterfly Wings","year":1995,"weight":21},{"id":222718485045440,"type":"song","name":"Cherub Rock","year":1993,"weight":21},{"id":216514219614843,"type":"song","name":"Rhinoceros","yea